1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,484
What if the ocean stopped moving for one minute?

2
00:00:03,524 --> 00:00:04,917
Waves are rolling in,

3
00:00:04,957 --> 00:00:06,964
gulls are screaming, and then,

4
00:00:07,004 --> 00:00:08,737
in the middle of a splash,

5
00:00:08,777 --> 00:00:10,033
every drop freezes.

6
00:00:10,073 --> 00:00:12,353
The whole sea goes still as glass.

7
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:15,569
People creep toward the shore.

8
00:00:15,609 --> 00:00:18,180
A surfer hangs in a perfect barrel wave,

9
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:20,204
frozen mid-ride, still smiling.

10
00:00:20,244 --> 00:00:21,509
Kids poke the water,

11
00:00:21,549 --> 00:00:22,946
and it doesn't ripple.

12
00:00:22,986 --> 00:00:24,186
It just sits there,

13
00:00:24,226 --> 00:00:25,753
like a giant blue jelly.

14
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:28,776
Then someone has an idea.

15
00:00:28,816 --> 00:00:31,743
They stand directly in front of the frozen

16
00:00:31,783 --> 00:00:33,368
wave and take a selfie.

17
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:36,264
Soon, the beach is crowded with tourists,

18
00:00:36,304 --> 00:00:38,878
all grinning in front of a giant blue

19
00:00:38,918 --> 00:00:39,867
wall of water.

20
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:43,740
At forty seconds, a scientist runs onto the

21
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:45,147
beach, waving her arms.

22
00:00:45,187 --> 00:00:46,554
If this wave unfreezes,

23
00:00:46,594 --> 00:00:49,062
she shouts, we need to be somewhere else.

24
00:00:49,102 --> 00:00:52,181
Everyone suddenly remembers what waves actually do.

25
00:00:53,450 --> 00:00:54,900
So the whole town runs uphill,

26
00:00:54,940 --> 00:00:58,326
carrying umbrellas, sandwiches, and one extremely confused dachshund.

27
00:00:58,366 --> 00:00:59,865
Meanwhile, the countdown ticks.

28
00:00:59,905 --> 00:01:02,696
Hypothetically, the ocean has never been so well-behaved.

29
00:01:03,850 --> 00:01:04,860
In a real world,

30
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:06,107
oceans can't pause.

31
00:01:06,147 --> 00:01:08,273
They carry far too much momentum,

32
00:01:08,313 --> 00:01:10,702
so this is only a thought experiment.

33
00:01:10,742 --> 00:01:12,212
But picture every tide,

34
00:01:12,252 --> 00:01:15,953
every current, and every wave holding its breath at once.

35
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:18,346
Here's the twist.

36
00:01:18,386 --> 00:01:20,751
At the very center of the stillness,

37
00:01:20,791 --> 00:01:24,226
a huge whale rises and sings one long, glowing note.

38
00:01:24,266 --> 00:01:25,830
The ocean wasn't frozen.

39
00:01:25,870 --> 00:01:27,567
It was stopping to listen.

40
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:29,954
Ten, nine, eight...

41
00:01:29,994 --> 00:01:31,002
The minute ends.

42
00:01:31,042 --> 00:01:33,228
The wave tumbles gently into foam,

43
00:01:33,268 --> 00:01:35,520
the sea sighs, and everyone cheers.

44
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:37,746
A single whale tail waves goodbye,

45
00:01:37,786 --> 00:01:40,496
and the ocean goes back to its usual song.
